From c33d01210d9276cfd542253f5ed7739db1cc76cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:32:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bt-reconnect: display on, music starting, a reboot, and no
 car kits

Earbuds do call back themselves when they leave their case, but their
attempt is short and when it misses it is not repeated (a pair of
earbuds on the Plinius, 2026-11-11: once connected within the second, an
hour earlier nothing reached BlueZ at all). Three more occasions for that:

- the display coming on, from MCE's display_status_ind
- a media player starting to play (MPRIS), the one moment that says the
  earbuds are wanted when the phone was in hand all along
- a restart: the candidate is kept in $XDG_STATE_HOME and taken over
  after a reboot, checked again against BlueZ

Only headphones and wearable headsets are dialled, by class of device: a
car kit calls itself audio-headset in BlueZ's Icon as well.

Without audioctl the service runs instead of being skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
